  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001134"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The city moved this case to its inactive list and shows it as Project Closed, last updated 2026-03-23. The city's data does not say how it was decided. Building application pending review.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001551"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier 59-unit, five-story condominium project on the site (preliminary application March 2016) was approved by the City Council in December 2019; Cresleigh recorded a subdivision map, demolished the buildings and remediated soil, but the approval expired. A 2023 extension request (PLN-2023-46) covered the 2016 approvals.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002958",
        "SRC-001551"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The site, about one acre between Dillon and Gilman Avenues, formerly held Paul del Grande Auto Parts and two homes and has been vacant since 2021.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002958",
        "SRC-002959"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the February 2026 hearing the applicant described 116 units; the staff report shows 90 units in the plans with an option up to 120. Building is about 75 feet tall with two levels of podium parking; 55 of 111 stalls with EV charging.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002957",
        "SRC-002958"
      ]
    }
  ],
